From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ThaRae <tharae@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:22:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] LibWebView: Don't let a page claim the browser's UI started a
 navigation

A navigation the browser's UI starts, from the address bar or a menu,
starts in the UI process. A page that asks the UI process to start or
continue a navigation can name it UserNavigationInvolvement::BrowserUI
all the same, and the UI process kept that claim: it re-derives the
initiator origin of the navigation, but copied user_involvement into
the canonical navigation's retry as it came. Anything that trusts the
retry's involvement then takes a compromised WebContent's word for it
that the user, not the page, asked for the navigation. Code that serves
a scheme only to navigations without a web initiator, for one, serves
it to the page.

No honest page sends that claim. Navigable::navigate() asserts that a
navigation with a source document is never BrowserUI, so a request to
navigate another navigable never carries it, and a link the page asks
the UI to open always uses Activation. The one page that starts a
BrowserUI navigation itself is the internals object's loadURL() of a
test.

So treat the claim as misbehavior in did_request_navigation_start()
outside of tests and WebDriver, and in did_request_navigation_of_
navigable() always, and ignore a link navigation that makes it.
---
 Libraries/LibWebView/WebContentPage.cpp | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Libraries/LibWebView/WebContentPage.cpp b/Libraries/LibWebView/WebContentPage.cpp
index e46b3e97fd4e06c3546053572967e055533c19b3..8bb4950911f212c47b486c6f8029ea36ba3e1c5f 100644
--- a/Libraries/LibWebView/WebContentPage.cpp
+++ b/Libraries/LibWebView/WebContentPage.cpp
@@ -721,6 +721,11 @@ static bool may_navigate_to_a_local_file(WebContentClient& requesting_client);
 
 void WebContentPage::did_request_navigation_of_navigable(Web::HTML::CrossProcessId navigable_id, Web::HTML::CrossProcessId source_navigable_id, Web::HTML::CrossProcessId source_document_id, Web::HTML::PreparedNavigationDescriptor navigation)
 {
+    if (navigation.user_involvement == Web::HTML::UserNavigationInvolvement::BrowserUI) {
+        client().did_misbehave("did_request_navigation_of_navigable"sv, "page claims the browser's UI started its navigation"sv);
+        return;
+    }
+
     if (navigation.url.scheme() == "file"sv && !may_navigate_to_a_local_file(client()))
         return;
 
@@ -1042,6 +1047,8 @@ static bool may_navigate_to_a_local_file(WebContentClient& requesting_client)
 // fetch client — as it does for a navigation the page starts itself, so a process names only a source it hosts.
 static Optional<Web::HTML::PreparedNavigationDescriptor> navigation_from_page(WebContentClient& requesting_client, Web::HTML::PreparedNavigationDescriptor navigation)
 {
+    if (navigation.user_involvement == Web::HTML::UserNavigationInvolvement::BrowserUI)
+        return {};
     // A page's own click or context menu names a document the page's process hosts, so only that process vouches for it.
     auto initiator_origin = initiator_origin_snapshot(navigation.initiator_origin_snapshot, navigation.source_snapshot_params, requesting_client);
     if (!initiator_origin.has_value())
@@ -2918,6 +2925,12 @@ void WebContentPage::did_request_navigation_start(Web::HTML::CrossProcessId navi
         client().did_misbehave("did_request_navigation_start"sv, "start request names another URL"sv);
         return;
     }
+    if (start_request.has_value()
+        && start_request->user_involvement == Web::HTML::UserNavigationInvolvement::BrowserUI
+        && !WebContentClient::renderers_may_synthesize_input()) {
+        client().did_misbehave("did_request_navigation_start"sv, "page claims the browser's UI started its navigation"sv);
+        return;
+    }
     if (start_request.has_value() && url.scheme() == "file"sv && !may_navigate_to_a_local_file(client())) {
         async_cancel_navigation_params_creation(navigable_id, navigation_id);
         return;
